      "knowledge_id": "unirank-method-infnet",
      "decision": "considered",
      "rationale": "Card, primary benchmark section2.3 line31 and pinned implementation forward123-170 inspected. Historical task-mask readouts are relevant nearest work, but the card does not establish local effectiveness. The local question comes from failed cubic/match-order trajectories and the incumbent primary uniform route; no hub architecture is adopted. Original INFNet full paper unavailable in the authorized text interface.",
      "transformed_mechanism": "No INFNet modules or hub/broadcast construction used. The candidate is a fixed union-feedback residual coefficient into existing task adapters, with aligned/rotated/duplicate/bridge controls.",
      "variant_names": [
        "feedback_aligned",
        "feedback_rotated",
        "feedback_gated_duplicate",
        "feedback_bridge"
      ],
      "nearest_work_difference": "Benchmark INFNet learns per-task mask-pooled projected hubs with layer-wise aggregation/broadcasting. This study fixes learned capacity and changes one coefficient direction, using a union mask. Novelty relative to the original method is unverified.",
      "falsifier": "Failure of aligned versus matched controls rejects this replacement, not INFNet or task-aware information flow in general.",
      "source_refs": [
        "unirank-benchmark-v2",
        "unirank-code:INFNet",
        "paper:infnet"
